      "id": "496f6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "Agreement Information The information below represents a view of articulated lower-division courses between California State University, Long Beach (CSULB) and the sending institution, aligning with the CSULB Academic Catalog. In the tables below, the left column represents CSULB courses, while any corresponding articulated courses are displayed on the right. It is essential to note that degree requirements may involve various combinations of courses or additional instructions; consequently, a careful review of all relevant information associated with the agreement is advised. Important Admissions Information for Fall 2027 ALL MAJORS ARE IMPACTED at California State University, Long Beach. As a result, incoming students must complete a series of major-specific preparation coursework and meet GPA requirements. Please visit our Major Specific Degree Requirements webpage for more information and to find the correct path and year for your major. Review the following for information related to transfer admissions to CSULB: Transfer Admission Eligibility Overview Transfer Application Process Lower Division Requirements Information for Major Agreements Due to ASSIST text limitations, some information regarding upper-division course options and electives may not be clear below. It is strongly recommended that agreement information along with CSULB Catalog information be reviewed when assessing a degree's requirements. It is crucial to note that the lower-division course requirements may change from year to year. The specific course requirements (catalog rights) will be determined for the student based on the catalog in effect at the time of their first term at CSULB. While effort is expended to mitigate alterations, agreement language can change with little advanced notice.",
      "contentHtml": "<h2>Agreement Information</h2><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">The information below represents a view of articulated lower-division courses between California State University, Long Beach (CSULB) and the sending institution, aligning with the CSULB Academic Catalog. In the tables below, the left column represents CSULB courses, while any corresponding articulated courses are displayed on the right. It is essential to note that degree requirements may involve various combinations of courses or additional instructions; consequently, a careful review of all relevant information associated with the agreement is advised.</p><p><br></p><h2>Important Admissions Information for Fall 2027</h2><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>ALL </strong><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/impaction-at-the-csu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>MAJORS ARE IMPACTED</strong></a> at California State University, Long Beach. As a result, incoming students <strong>must</strong> complete a series of major-specific preparation coursework and meet GPA requirements. Please visit our <a href=\"https://www.csulb.edu/admissions/major-specific-degree-requirements-for-transfer-students\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Major Specific Degree Requirements</a> webpage for more information and to find the correct path and year for your major.</p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\"><br></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review the following for information related to transfer admissions to CSULB:</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><a href=\"https://www.csulb.edu/admissions/transfer-admission-eligibility\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admission Eligibility Overview</a></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><a href=\"https://www.csulb.edu/admissions/transfer-application-process\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Application Process</a></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><a href=\"https://www.csulb.edu/academic-affairs/articulation/assist-agreement-information\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Lower Division Requirements Information for Major Agreements</a></li></ul><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\">Due to ASSIST text limitations, some information regarding upper-division course options and electives may not be clear below. It is strongly recommended that agreement information <strong>along with</strong> <a href=\"https://csulb.catalog.acalog.com/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSULB Catalog information</a> be reviewed when assessing a degree's requirements. It is crucial to note that the lower-division course requirements may change from year to year. The specific course requirements (catalog rights) will be determined for the student based on the catalog in effect at the time of their first term at CSULB. While effort is expended to mitigate alterations, agreement language can change with little advanced notice.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "0eb56845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "GENERAL INFORMATION & DEGREE NOTES",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0cb56845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "Foreign Language: Take at least three semesters (or the equivalent) of a single Asian language. Language choices are Chinese, Japanese, or an Asian language approved by the undergraduate advisor (typically Korean, Vietnamese, or Cambodian). Those with an Asian language competency may test out of this requirement. Contact the Asian Studies Department for further information. Department Recommendation: Since statistics and economics are important for this major, students are advised to take ECON 101 or STAT 108 as part of their general education requirements. Consult the CSULB Catalog and the Asian Studies Department for additional details.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Foreign Language: Take at least three semesters (or the equivalent) of a single Asian language. Language choices are Chinese, Japanese, or an Asian language approved by the undergraduate advisor (typically Korean, Vietnamese, or Cambodian). Those with an Asian language competency may test out of this requirement. <strong>Contact </strong>the Asian Studies Department for further information.</p><p><br></p><p>Department Recommendation: Since statistics and economics are important for this major, students are advised to take ECON 101 or STAT 108 as part of their general education requirements.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Consult</strong> the <a href=\"https://csulb.catalog.acalog.com/preview_program.php?catoid=12&amp;poid=6229\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSULB Catalog</a> and the <a href=\"https://cla.csulb.edu/departments/aaas/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Asian Studies Department</a> for additional details.</p>"
    }
  ],
